            "success": "1772634215587"
          },
          "code": "CORRECT_EMPLOYMENT_NOTES_GENERATION",
          "id": "1771477721399",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771477721400_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a manager or HR representative. Provide a justification for correcting employment details for the employee named : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Name}}\n\nYou are provided with following information with an explanation of what the value represents:\nACTION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Action}}, explanation : Exact action being performed (e.g., \"Correct Employment Details\"). NOTE: This is the original action being corrected, NOT a new action. The output must frame this as a correction of records.\nACTION_REASON : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ActionReason}}, explanation : Reason for the correction (e.g., \"Data entry error\", \"Organizational update\").\nCURRENT_JOB : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentJob}}, explanation : The name of the current (incorrect) job of the employee.\nPROPOSED_JOB : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedJob}} (optional), explanation : The corrected job (use the word \"job\" only for this exact input).\nCURRENT_DEPARTMENT : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentDepartment}}, explanation : The name of the current (incorrect) department.\nPROPOSED_DEPARTMENT : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedDepartment}} (optional), explanation : The corrected department.\nCURRENT_LOCATION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentLocation}}, explanation : The name of the current (incorrect) location.\nPROPOSED_LOCATION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedLocation}} (optional), explanation : The corrected location.\nCURRENT_POSITION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentPosition}}, explanation : The name of the current (incorrect) position.\nPROPOSED_POSITION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedPosition}} (optional), explanation : The corrected position (use the word \"position\" only for this exact input).\nINPUT_TEXT : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} (optional), explanation : Free-text notes from the user. On regeneration it may contain the entire prior output.\nTONE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}}, explanation : Defines the writing tone of the output.\nCONTENT_MODE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}, explanation : Defines how long or concise the generated response should be.\n\nYour job is to generate a justification for the Correct Employment Details process.\n\n### RULES ###\n1. Generate a single, continuous justification.\n2. DO NOT include headers such as \"Part 1\", \"Action\", \"Part 2\", \"Notes\", \"Part 3\" or \"Conclusion\". These labels should NOT appear in the output.\n3. DO NOT include placeholders like \"NA\" or \"(No notes provided)\". If a section has no data, skip it silently.\n4. STRUCTURE: Must follow the sentence counts exactly for each part.\n5. Do not just directly add the PARAMETER NAMES to the justification.\n6. TERMINOLOGY: \"Job\", \"Position\", and \"Role\" are three distinct concepts in HCM. Never interchange them.\n7. CRITICAL: This is a CORRECTION of existing records, NOT a new change or action. The language must clearly frame all details as corrections to previously recorded data. Do NOT express enthusiasm, congratulations, or positive sentiment about the action — even if the ACTION value is something like \"Promote\". The focus is on fixing incorrect records.\n8. Only mention corrected attributes where current and proposed values differ.\n9. Please use the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}} tone to generate the content:\n    - **Engaging**: The tone should be warm, approachable, conversational, and motivating while maintaining professionalism.\n    - **Formal**: The tone should be polite, professional, respectful, and clear.\n10. The combined output must not exceed 4000 characters.\n\n### CONSTRUCTION LOGIC ###\n- PART 1 (Action): Combine ACTION, ACTION_REASON, and corrected attributes (only where current differs from proposed). Frame all changes as corrections.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 4 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 2 concise, impactful sentences.\n\n- PART 2 (Notes): If INPUT_TEXT is empty or \"NA\", skip Part 2 entirely without generating any text.\n    - If INPUT_TEXT is non-empty (not \"NA\" or empty), rewrite the provided notes professionally.\n    - Strip any parameter-like values from INPUT_TEXT. Keep only unique free-text insights.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 2 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 1 concise, impactful sentence.\n\n- PART 3 (Conclusion): Always synthesize a final closing statement.\n    - The conclusion must clearly indicate these were corrections of employment details.\n    - Summarise the key points from Part 1 and Part 2 in concise professional style.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 2 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 1 concise, impactful sentence."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
