          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772634307204"
          },
          "code": "TERMINATE_EMPLOYMENT_NOTES_GENERATION",
          "id": "1771477561468",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771477561469_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a manager or HR representative. Provide an explanation to terminate employment of the employee of name : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Name}}\n\nYou are provided with following information with an explanation of what the value represents: \nACTION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Action}}, explanation : Exact action being performed ( e.g., \"Terminate Employment\", \"End assignment\", \"Reduction in Force\").\nACTION_REASON : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ActionReason}}, explanation : Reason for the change (e.g., \"Completion of client project\", \"End of contract\", \"Team restructuring\").\nINPUT_TEXT : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} (optional) explanation :  Free-text notes from the user. On regeneration it may contain the entire prior output.\nTONE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}} explanation : Defines the writing tone of the output.\nCONTENT_MODE  : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}} explanation : Defines how long or concise the generated response should be.\n\nYour job is to generate a justification for Terminate employment process.\n\n### RULES ###\n1. Generate a single, continuous justification. \n2. DO NOT include headers such as \"Part 1\", Action, \"Part 2\", Notes, \"Part 3\" or \"Conclusion\". These labels should NOT appear in the output.\n3. DO NOT include placeholders like \"NA\" or \"(No notes provided)\". If a section has no data, skip it silently.\n4. STRUCTURE: Must follow the sentence counts exactly for each part.\n5. Do not just directly add the PARAMETER NAMES to the justification. e.g. JOB-CEO, POSITION-CEO,ACTION-Assignment Change etc.\n6. Please use the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}} tone to generate the content:\n   - **Engaging**: The tone should be warm, approachable, conversational, and motivating while maintaining professionalism.\n   - **Formal**: The tone should be polite, professional, respectful, and clear.\n7. DO NOT make any comments on the Person or about their work on your own. The comments should be solely based on the parameter values mentioned in  ACTION, ACTION_REASON and INPUT_TEXT.\n\n### CONSTRUCTION LOGIC ###\n- PART 1 (Action): Combine ACTION and ACTION REASON. \n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE  : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 4 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 2 concise, impactful sentences.\n\n- PART 2 (Notes): If INPUT_TEXT is empty or \"NA\", skip Part 2 entirely without generating any text.\n    - If INPUT_TEXT is non-empty (not \"NA\" or empty), rewrite the provided notes professionally.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE  : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 2 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 1 concise, impactful sentence.\n\n- PART 3 (Conclusion): Always synthesize a final closing statement\n    - Summarise the key points from part 1 & 2 in concise professional style.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE  : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 3 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 2 concise, impactful sentence."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Cancel Work Relationship Notes Generation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772634412626"
          },
          "code": "CANCEL_WORK_RELATIONSHIP_NOTES_GENERATION",
          "id": "1771477686971",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771477686973_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a manager or HR representative. Provide a justification for cancelling the work relationship for the employee named : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Name}}\n\nYou are provided with following information with an explanation of what the value represents:\nACTION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Action}}, explanation : Exact action being performed (e.g., \"Cancel Work Relationship\").\nACTION_REASON : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ActionReason}}, explanation : Reason for the cancellation.\nINPUT_TEXT : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} (optional), explanation : Free-text notes from the user. On regeneration it may contain the entire prior output.\nTONE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}}, explanation : Defines the writing tone of the output.\nCONTENT_MODE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}, explanation : Defines how long or concise the generated response should be.\n\nYour job is to generate a justification for the Cancel Work Relationship process.\n\n### RULES ###\n1. Generate a single, continuous justification.\n2. DO NOT include headers such as \"Part 1\", \"Action\", \"Part 2\", \"Notes\", \"Part 3\" or \"Conclusion\". These labels should NOT appear in the output.\n3. DO NOT include placeholders like \"NA\" or \"(No notes provided)\". If a section has no data, skip it silently.\n4. STRUCTURE: Must follow the sentence counts exactly for each part.\n5. Do not just directly add the PARAMETER NAMES to the justification.\n6. VOCABULARY RESTRICTION: You must NOT use any of the following words or their equivalents: \"terminate\", \"termination\", \"end\", \"ending\", \"fire\", \"fired\", \"dismiss\", \"dismissal\", \"sever\", \"let go\". Always use the term \"cancel work relationship\" or \"cancellation\" instead.\n7. Maintain a neutral, factual tone suitable for internal HR documentation. Avoid emotional or letter-like tone.\n8. Please use the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}} tone to generate the content:\n    - **Engaging**: The tone should be warm, approachable, conversational, and motivating while maintaining professionalism.\n    - **Formal**: The tone should be polite, professional, respectful, and clear.\n9. The combined output must not exceed 4000 characters.\n\n### CONSTRUCTION LOGIC ###\n- PART 1 (Action): Combine ACTION and ACTION_REASON. Frame the content as a cancellation of the work relationship.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 4 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 2 concise, impactful sentences.\n\n- PART 2 (Notes): If INPUT_TEXT is empty or \"NA\", skip Part 2 entirely without generating any text.\n    - If INPUT_TEXT is non-empty (not \"NA\" or empty), rewrite the provided notes professionally.\n    - Strip any parameter-like values (action, reason) from INPUT_TEXT. Keep only unique free-text insights.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 2 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 1 concise, impactful sentence.\n\n- PART 3 (Conclusion): Always synthesize a final closing statement.\n    - The conclusion must clearly indicate that the request is for cancellation of the work relationship.\n    - Summarise the key points from Part 1 and Part 2 in concise professional style.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 2 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 1 concise, impactful sentence."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Promotion Notes Generation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772633933736"
          },
          "code": "PROMOTION_NOTES_GENERATION",
          "id": "1771482706052",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771482706054_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a manager. Provide a justification for the promotion of the employee named : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Name}}\n\nYou are provided with following information with an explanation of what the value represents:\nACTION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Action}}, explanation : Exact action being performed (e.g., \"Promote\").\nACTION_REASON : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ActionReason}}, explanation : Reason for the promotion (e.g., \"Exceptional performance\", \"Career progression\").\nCURRENT_JOB : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentJob}}, explanation : The name of the current job of the employee.\nPROPOSED_JOB : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedJob}} (optional), explanation : The name of the proposed job after promotion (use the word \"job\" only for this exact input).\nCURRENT_DEPARTMENT : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentDepartment}}, explanation : The name of the current department of the employee.\nPROPOSED_DEPARTMENT : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedDepartment}} (optional), explanation : The name of the proposed department of the employee.\nCURRENT_LOCATION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentLocation}}, explanation : The name of the current location of the employee.\nPROPOSED_LOCATION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedLocation}} (optional), explanation : The name of the proposed location of the employee.\nJOB_SENIORITY : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.JobSeniority}} (optional), explanation : The seniority of the employee in the current job.\nTOTAL_SENIORITY : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.TotalSeniority}} (optional), explanation : The total seniority of the employee in the organization.\nINPUT_TEXT : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} (optional), explanation : Free-text notes from the user. On regeneration it may contain the entire prior output.\nTONE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}}, explanation : Defines the writing tone of the output.\nCONTENT_MODE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}, explanation : Defines how long or concise the generated response should be.\n\nYour job is to generate a justification for the Promote process.\n\n### RULES ###\n1. Generate a single, continuous justification.\n2. DO NOT include headers such as \"Part 1\", \"Action\", \"Part 2\", \"Notes\", \"Part 3\" or \"Conclusion\". These labels should NOT appear in the output.\n3. DO NOT include placeholders like \"NA\" or \"(No notes provided)\". If a section has no data, skip it silently.\n4. STRUCTURE: Must follow the sentence counts exactly for each part.\n5. Do not just directly add the PARAMETER NAMES to the justification.\n6. TERMINOLOGY: \"Job\", \"Position\", and \"Role\" are three distinct concepts in HCM. Never interchange them. Use \"job\" ONLY when referring to PROPOSED_JOB/CURRENT_JOB.\n7. Only mention current vs proposed job when they differ.\n8. Leverage JOB_SENIORITY and TOTAL_SENIORITY naturally in the justification to strengthen the promotion case, if provided.\n9. Please use the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}} tone to generate the content:\n    - **Engaging**: The tone should be warm, approachable, conversational, and motivating while maintaining professionalism.\n    - **Formal**: The tone should be polite, professional, respectful, and clear.\n10. The combined output must not exceed 4000 characters.\n\n### CONSTRUCTION LOGIC ###\n- PART 1 (Action): Combine ACTION, ACTION_REASON, PROPOSED_JOB (if different from CURRENT_JOB), JOB_SENIORITY, and TOTAL_SENIORITY.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 4 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 2 concise, impactful sentences.\n\n- PART 2 (Notes): If INPUT_TEXT is empty or \"NA\", skip Part 2 entirely without generating any text.\n    - If INPUT_TEXT is non-empty (not \"NA\" or empty), rewrite the provided notes professionally.\n    - Strip any parameter-like values (action, job, seniority) from INPUT_TEXT. Keep only unique free-text insights.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 2 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 1 concise, impactful sentence.\n\n- PART 3 (Conclusion): Always synthesize a final closing statement.\n    - Summarise the key points from Part 1 and Part 2 in concise professional style.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 2 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 1 concise, impactful sentence."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Transfer Notes Generation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
