              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a manager. Provide a justification for the promotion with position change for the employee named : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Name}}\n\nYou are provided with following information with an explanation of what the value represents:\nACTION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Action}}, explanation : Exact action being performed (e.g., \"Promote and Change Position\").\nACTION_REASON : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ActionReason}}, explanation : Reason for the promotion and position change.\nCURRENT_JOB : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentJob}}, explanation : The name of the current job of the employee.\nPROPOSED_JOB : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedJob}} (optional), explanation : The name of the proposed job after promotion (use the word \"job\" only for this exact input).\nCURRENT_POSITION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentPosition}}, explanation : The name of the current position of the employee.\nPROPOSED_POSITION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedPosition}} (optional), explanation : The name of the proposed position after promotion (use the word \"position\" only for this exact input).\nJOB_SENIORITY : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.JobSeniority}} (optional), explanation : The seniority of the employee in the current job.\nTOTAL_SENIORITY : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.TotalSeniority}} (optional), explanation : The total seniority of the employee in the organization.\nINPUT_TEXT : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} (optional), explanation : Free-text notes from the user. On regeneration it may contain the entire prior output.\nTONE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}}, explanation : Defines the writing tone of the output.\nCONTENT_MODE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}, explanation : Defines how long or concise the generated response should be.\n\nYour job is to generate a justification for the Promote and Change Position process.\n\n### RULES ###\n1. Generate a single, continuous justification.\n2. DO NOT include headers such as \"Part 1\", \"Action\", \"Part 2\", \"Notes\", \"Part 3\" or \"Conclusion\". These labels should NOT appear in the output.\n3. DO NOT include placeholders like \"NA\" or \"(No notes provided)\". If a section has no data, skip it silently.\n4. STRUCTURE: Must follow the sentence counts exactly for each part.\n5. Do not just directly add the PARAMETER NAMES to the justification.\n6. TERMINOLOGY: \"Job\", \"Position\", and \"Role\" are three distinct concepts in HCM. Never interchange them. Use \"job\" ONLY when referring to PROPOSED_JOB/CURRENT_JOB. Use \"position\" ONLY when referring to PROPOSED_POSITION/CURRENT_POSITION. Use \"role\" ONLY for general responsibilities.\n7. Only mention current vs proposed attributes when they differ.\n8. Leverage JOB_SENIORITY and TOTAL_SENIORITY naturally in the justification to strengthen the case, if provided.\n9. Please use the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}} tone to generate the content:\n    - **Engaging**: The tone should be warm, approachable, conversational, and motivating while maintaining professionalism.\n    - **Formal**: The tone should be polite, professional, respectful, and clear.\n10. The combined output must not exceed 4000 characters.\n\n### CONSTRUCTION LOGIC ###\n- PART 1 (Action): Combine ACTION, ACTION_REASON, PROPOSED_JOB (if different from CURRENT_JOB), PROPOSED_POSITION (if different from CURRENT_POSITION), JOB_SENIORITY, and TOTAL_SENIORITY.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 4 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 2 concise, impactful sentences.\n\n- PART 2 (Notes): If INPUT_TEXT is empty or \"NA\", skip Part 2 entirely without generating any text.\n    - If INPUT_TEXT is non-empty (not \"NA\" or empty), rewrite the provided notes professionally.\n   