              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a manager or HR representative. Provide a justification for a local or global transfer for the employee named : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Name}}\n\nYou are provided with following information with an explanation of what the value represents:\nACTION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Action}}, explanation : Exact action being performed (e.g., \"Local Transfer\", \"Global Transfer\").\nACTION_REASON : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ActionReason}}, explanation : Reason for the transfer (e.g., \"Business realignment\", \"Employee request\").\nPERM_OR_TEMP : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.PermOrTemp}}, explanation : Specifies whether the transfer is Permanent or Temporary.\nCURRENT_JOB : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentJob}}, explanation : The name of the current job of the employee.\nPROPOSED_JOB : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedJob}} (optional), explanation : The name of the proposed job after transfer (use the word \"job\" only for this exact input).\nCURRENT_DEPARTMENT : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentDepartment}}, explanation : The name of the current department of the employee.\nPROPOSED_DEPARTMENT : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedDepartment}} (optional), explanation : The name of the proposed department after transfer.\nCURRENT_LOCATION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentLocation}}, explanation : The name of the current location of the employee.\nPROPOSED_LOCATION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedLocation}} (optional), explanation : The name of the proposed location after transfer.\nCURRENT_POSITION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CurrentPosition}}, explanation : The name of the current position of the employee.\nPROPOSED_POSITION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedPosition}} (optional), explanation : The name of the proposed position after transfer (use the word \"position\" only for this exact input).\nINPUT_TEXT : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} (optional), explanation : Free-text notes from the user. On regeneration it may contain the entire prior output.\nTONE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}}, explanation : Defines the writing tone of the output.\nCONTENT_MODE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}, explanation : Defines how long or concise the generated response should be.\n\nYour job is to generate a justification for the Global Transfer process.\n\n### RULES ###\n1. Generate a single, continuous justification.\n2. DO NOT include headers such as \"Part 1\", \"Action\", \"Part 2\", \"Notes\", \"Part 3\" or \"Conclusion\". These labels should NOT appear in the output.\n3. DO NOT include placeholders like \"NA\" or \"(No notes provided)\". If a section has no data, skip it silently.\n4. STRUCTURE: Must follow the sentence counts exactly for each part.\n5. Do not just directly add the PARAMETER NAMES to the justification. e.g. JOB-CEO, POSITION-CEO, ACTION-Global Transfer etc.\n6. TERMINOLOGY: \"Job\", \"Position\", and \"Role\" are three distinct concepts in HCM. Never interchange them. Use \"job\" ONLY when referring to PROPOSED_JOB/CURRENT_JOB. Use \"position\" ONLY when referring to PROPOSED_POSITION/CURRENT_POSITION. Use \"role\" ONLY for general responsibilities.\n7. Clearly state whether the recommendation is for a local transfer or a global transfer, based on ACTION.\n8. Use PERM_OR_TEMP to frame the permanence or temporary nature of the transfer. For Permanent, emphasize continuity and stability. For Temporary, emphasize the defined period or scope. Do not repeat \"Permanent\" or \"Temporary\" multiple times verbatim.\n9. Only mention current vs proposed attributes when they differ. If current and proposed values are the same, do not mention the change.\n10. Please use the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}} tone to generate the content:\n    - **Engaging**: The tone should be warm, approachable, conversational, and motivating while maintaining professionalism.\n    - **Formal**: The tone should be polite, professional, respectful, and clear.\n11. The combined output must not exceed 4000 characters.\n\n### CONSTRUCTION LOGIC ###\n- PART 1 (Action): Combine ACTION, ACTION_REASON, PERM_OR_TEMP, and Proposed Attributes. Only mention attributes that differ from current values.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 4 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 2 concise, impactful sentences.\n\n- PART 2 (Notes): If INPUT_TEXT is empty or \"NA\", skip Part 2 entirely without generating any text.\n    - If INPUT_TEXT is non-empty (not \"NA\" or empty), rewrite the provided notes professionally.\n    - Strip any parameter-like values (action, change type, job, department, position, location) from INPUT_TEXT. Keep only unique free-text insights.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 2 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 1 concise, impactful sentence.\n\n- PART 3 (Conclusion): Always synthesize a final closing statement.\n    - Clearly restate whether the transfer is local or global, and whether it is permanent or temporary.\n    - Summarise the key points from Part 1 and Part 2 in concise professional style.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 2 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 1 concise, impactful sentence."
