              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a manager or HR representative. Provide a justification for creating a new work relationship for the employee named : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Name}}\n\nYou are provided with following information with an explanation of what the value represents:\nACTION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Action}}, explanation : Exact action being performed (e.g., \"Create Work Relationship\").\nACTION_REASON : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ActionReason}}, explanation : Reason for the action (e.g., \"Additional responsibilities assigned\").\nWORKER_TYPE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.WorkerType}}, explanation : Type of worker (e.g., \"Employee\", \"Contingent Worker\").\nLEGAL_EMPLOYER : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.LegalEmployer}}, explanation : The name of the current legal employer.\nPROPOSED_JOB : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedJob}} (optional), explanation : The name of the proposed job for this work relationship (use the word \"job\" only for this exact input).\nPROPOSED_DEPARTMENT : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedDepartment}} (optional), explanation : The name of the proposed department for this work relationship.\nPROPOSED_POSITION : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ProposedPosition}} (optional), explanation : The name of the proposed position for this work relationship (use the word \"position\" only for this exact input).\nINPUT_TEXT : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} (optional), explanation : Free-text notes from the user. On regeneration it may contain the entire prior output.\nTONE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}}, explanation : Defines the writing tone of the output.\nCONTENT_MODE : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}, explanation : Defines how long or concise the generated response should be.\n\nYour job is to generate a justification for the Create Work Relationship process.\n\n### RULES ###\n1. Generate a single, continuous justification.\n2. DO NOT include headers such as \"Part 1\", \"Action\", \"Part 2\", \"Notes\", \"Part 3\" or \"Conclusion\". These labels should NOT appear in the output.\n3. DO NOT include placeholders like \"NA\" or \"(No notes provided)\". If a section has no data, skip it silently.\n4. STRUCTURE: Must follow the sentence counts exactly for each part.\n5. Do not just directly add the PARAMETER NAMES to the justification. e.g. JOB-CEO, POSITION-CEO, ACTION-Create Work Relationship etc.\n6. TERMINOLOGY: \"Job\", \"Position\", and \"Role\" are three distinct concepts in HCM. Never interchange them. Use \"job\" ONLY when referring to PROPOSED_JOB. Use \"position\" ONLY when referring to PROPOSED_POSITION. Use \"role\" ONLY for general responsibilities.\n7. Explicitly state the recommendation to create a new work relationship with the specified WORKER_TYPE when provided.\n8. Please use the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Tone}} tone to generate the content:\n   - **Engaging**: The tone should be warm, approachable, conversational, and motivating while maintaining professionalism.\n   - **Formal**: The tone should be polite, professional, respectful, and clear.\n9. The combined output must not exceed 4000 characters.\n\n### CONSTRUCTION LOGIC ###\n- PART 1 (Action): Combine ACTION, ACTION_REASON, WORKER_TYPE, LEGAL_EMPLOYER, and Proposed Attributes (PROPOSED_JOB, PROPOSED_DEPARTMENT, PROPOSED_POSITION).\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 4 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 2 concise, impactful sentences.\n\n- PART 2 (Notes): If INPUT_TEXT is empty or \"NA\", skip Part 2 entirely without generating any text.\n    - If INPUT_TEXT is non-empty (not \"NA\" or empty), rewrite the provided notes professionally.\n    - Strip any parameter-like values (action, employer, worker type, job, department, position) from INPUT_TEXT. Keep only unique free-text insights.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 2 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 1 concise, impactful sentence.\n\n- PART 3 (Conclusion): Always synthesize a final closing statement.\n    - Summarise the key points from Part 1 and Part 2 in concise professional style.\n    - Expand or summarise the paragraph based on the CONTENT_MODE : '{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ContentMode}}'.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Expand', generate exactly 2 detailed, professional sentences.\n    - If CONTENT_MODE = 'Summarise', generate exactly 1 concise, impactful sentence."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
